      "<p>The <strong>Kanchenjunga Circuit Trek</strong> is the definitive expedition-scale trek in eastern Nepal, linking both base camps of <strong>Kanchenjunga (8,586 m)</strong> — the world's third-highest mountain — in a single 21-day journey. The route flies to Bhadrapur, drives up through the tea gardens of Ilam to Taplejung, and walks north up the Tamor valley through subtropical forest into high glacial country.</p><p>The northern arm reaches <strong>Pangpema (5,143 m)</strong> beneath the immense north face, then crosses the <strong>Sele La</strong> ridge system to the southern side for the Oktang viewpoint above the Yalung Glacier. Between them lie the Sherpa village of Ghunsa, the high camps at Kambachen and Lhonak, and some of the least visited high country in Nepal. This is a restricted region and a genuinely remote undertaking.</p>",
